'freely transferable' is a factual question to be determined on the basis of all
relevant facts and circumstances," and provides several examples of restrictions
on transferability that, absent unusual circumstances, will not prevent the
rights of ownership in question from being considered "freely transferable" if
the minimum investment is $10,000 or less. The allowed restrictions in the
examples are illustrative of restrictions commonly found in public real estate
limited partnerships that are imposed to comply with state and federal law, to
assure continued eligibility for favorable tax treatment and to avoid certain
